WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.970
Every good story has a beginning, a middle and an end. Code can tell stories too!

2
00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:08.700
Meet the character.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.100
“Once upon a time, there was a little fox.”

4
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.780
Something happens!

5
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.780
The fox goes on a trip or finds a problem.

6
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.310
How it finishes.

7
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.870
“And the fox went home happy.

8
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.660
The end!”

9
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:32.610
Your blocks follow the story order: beginning blocks first, end blocks last.

10
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:40.230
Beginning: say “Once upon a time”. Middle: walk to the berry (gem) and pick it. End: say “The end!”.

11
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.640
Beginning, middle, end — a complete story!

12
00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.490
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

13
00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:54.160
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
